      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.05,
          "end": 5.16,
          "en": "Now GitHub Copilot and GitHub Copilot Chat",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.16,
          "end": 10.16,
          "en": "were useful extensions for existing code editors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.38,
          "end": 13.83,
          "en": "The last tool we'll explore in this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.83,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "is a code editor on its own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 20.37,
          "en": "The Cursor IDE is a fork",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.37,
          "end": 24.87,
          "en": "so you could say a copy of the Visual Studio Code editor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.87,
          "end": 29.13,
          "en": "but it is a copy that puts AI first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 29.13,
          "end": 34.13,
          "en": "that integrates AI into the very core of the editor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 35.22,
          "end": 39.99,
          "en": "This Cursor IDE, as you will see over the next lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 39.99,
          "end": 44.99,
          "en": "is all about prompt-focused, AI-driven programming.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 45.66,
          "end": 47.52,
          "en": "You'll still write code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 47.52,
          "end": 50.79,
          "en": "it's still an editor for developers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 50.79,
          "end": 54.75,
          "en": "but you'll also write a lot of AI instructions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 54.75,
          "end": 57.27,
          "en": "And as you'll see throughout the next lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 57.27,
          "end": 61.47,
          "en": "often your main job as a developer simply is to tweak",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 61.47,
          "end": 64.51,
          "en": "and control the code that is generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 65.52,
          "end": 69.45,
          "en": "because this editor is able to generate, explain,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 69.45,
          "end": 71.37,
          "en": "enhance, and fix code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 71.37,
          "end": 73.68,
          "en": "and also search official documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 73.68,
          "end": 78.06,
          "en": "and do more all from inside the editor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 78.06,
          "end": 81.27,
          "en": "without opening some extra chat sidebar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 81.27,
          "end": 84.69,
